    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72369" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴκο-τριψ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐβος</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a slave born and bred in the house,</i>
			
				Att.
			 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκογενής</span> (<i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				590.15
			</span></i>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰ. κλώψ,</span> of a mouse
			(cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκόσιτος</span> II), <i><span class="en">
				Babr.
				107.2
			</span></i> ; as a term of abuse, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾡκότριψ Εὐριπίδης</span>”
				<i>the slave</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				426
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκοτρίβων οἰκότριβας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					13.24
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετὰ τῶν οἰ. παίζειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>VH</u>
					12.15
				</span></i>
			 : metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκότριβες ἐν φιλοσοφίᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Acad.Ind.</u>
					p.19M.
				</span></i>
			</div>
